3. Runtime pseudocode

3.1 Initialization

function DTDT.init(config):
    state = config.initial_state
    params = init_autodidact_params(config.autodidact_params)
    mode_schedule = config.mode_schedule
    current_mode = mode_schedule[0].mode
    time_index = 0
    log = empty_trajectory_log()
    keys = load_key_hierarchy("C.MATTHEW.BLACKWELL/INDEPENDENT.DESIGNER")

    return Handle(state, params, mode_schedule, current_mode, time_index, log, keys)

3.2 Single step

function DTDT.step(handle):
    if handle.current_mode == STOP:
        return StepResult(handle.state, STOP, true, null)

    if handle.current_mode == PAUSE:
        record = record_noop_transition(handle)
        append(handle.log, record)
        return StepResult(handle.state, PAUSE, false, record)

    # 1. Forward step
    state_f = MetaKernelF.forward(handle.state, handle.params, handle.env)

    # 2. Reverse step
    state_r = MetaKernelR.reverse(handle.state, handle.params, handle.env)

    # 3. Convergence check
    if Convergence.is_consistent(state_f, state_r):
        state_star = Convergence.merge(state_f, state_r)
        handle.state = state_star
        handle.current_mode = INSTANT
        record = record_transition(handle.state, state_star, handle.current_mode)
        sign_transition(record, handle.keys)
        append(handle.log, record)
        return StepResult(state_star, INSTANT, true, record)

    # 4. Normal dual update
    new_state = TemporalEngine.combine(state_f, state_r, handle.current_mode)
    record = record_transition(handle.state, new_state, handle.current_mode)
    sign_transition(record, handle.keys)
    append(handle.log, record)

    # 5. Autodidact learning update
    handle.params = Autodidact.update(handle.params, handle.state, new_state)

    handle.state = new_state
    handle.time_index += 1
    handle.current_mode = TemporalEngine.next_mode(handle.mode_schedule, handle.time_index)

    return StepResult(handle.state, handle.current_mode, false, record)

3.3 Full run

function DTDT.run(handle):
    while true:
        step = DTDT.step(handle)
        if step.converged or handle.current_mode == STOP:
            break

    result = DTDTRunResult(
        final_state = handle.state,
        trajectory_log = handle.log,
        disagreement_map = build_disagreement_map(handle.log),
        mode_log = extract_mode_log(handle.log),
        signatures = collect_signatures(handle.log)
    )

    sign_run(result, handle.keys)
    return result

4. Encryption key hierarchy

4.1 Identity root

Root namespace:C.MATTHEW.BLACKWELL/INDEPENDENT.DESIGNER

Root keypair:

RootPrivateKey — offline, never used directly at runtime

RootPublicKey — used to verify all subordinate keys

4.2 Derived keys

Engine key

ID: DTDT_ENGINE_KEY

Purpose: sign engine‑level events (run start, run end)

Derived from root via deterministic KDF.

Transition key

ID: DTDT_TRANSITION_KEY

Purpose: sign each state transition S_t → S_{t+1}

Rotatable per run or per N steps.

Mode key

ID: DTDT_MODE_KEY

Purpose: sign mode changes (Alpha → Omega → etc.)

Log key

ID: DTDT_LOG_KEY

Purpose: sign exported trajectory logs.

4.3 Signing scheme

Transition signing

function sign_transition(record, keys):
    payload = hash(record.previous_state, record.next_state, record.mode, record.timestamp)
    record.signature = sign(payload, keys.transition_key)

Run signing

function sign_run(result, keys):
    payload = hash(result.final_state, result.trajectory_log, result.mode_log)
    result.run_signature = sign(payload, keys.engine_key)

